	(footprint "duck-jaws-local:LED_LiteOn_LTST-S270_SideView"
		(layer "B.Cu")
		(uuid "9e9a6ae2-9305-40f7-884a-04cfb1b5e4fd")
		(at 223.3226 81.6069 180)
		(descr "Side-firing single-colour chip LED, Lite-On LTST-S270 family (SAOPP-LED-01..05; red LTST-S270KRKT is LCSC C125114). Body 1.65 long, 0.60 high, 1.15 deep (0.68 terminal block plus a 1.20 wide lens that sticks out 0.47). Land pattern from the datasheet's 'Suggest Soldering Pad Dimensions' (https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C125114.pdf, sheet 7 of 12, read 2026-11-11): two pads 1.10 x 1.10 mm, 0.90 mm apart. The lens points toward +Y of this footprint. Pad 1 = cathode, pad 2 = anode. The drawing does not dimension the pads against the body: the terminal block is drawn centred on the pads, which is an estimate. Kept in this board's folder until the shared library has a footprint for LED-01.")
